      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Natural stone, like marble or granite, is the most luxurious and prestigious option, fitting perfectly for a high-end law firm in London. It exudes an air of timeless authority, but it is also the most fragile of the three, easily scratching or etching if a goblin were to drop a heavy iron pot on it. It requires careful sealing and polishing to maintain its luster, or it will look like a dusty, cracked goblin's cave.\n\nHere is a quick summary of the maintenance needs for each material:\n\n| Material | Maintenance Requirements | Long-Term Wear & Tear |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Polished Concrete** | Regular sweeping, damp mopping, and periodic resealing (every 1-2 years). | **High Durability:** Resists heavy traffic, impacts, and scratches best. Can stain if not sealed properly. |\n| **Luxury Vinyl Tile (LVT)** | Easy daily cleaning with a damp mop; avoid harsh chemicals. | **Medium Durability:** Resists moisture and wear well, but can be scratched by sharp objects or dragged furniture. |\n| **Natural Stone** | Requires daily sweeping, damp mopping, and professional sealing",
